  "implemented": [
    "Exact public task ID and safe relative path retain literal task/group/Captain workspaces. Public requests carry no root, path authority, document lease, callback receipt, nonce or clipboard contents.",
    "Actual bounded SQL scopes and task/project/group/assigned agent read grants are captured and rechecked. Live agents continue without metadata mutation or task/session events; credential/full task getters are not used for copy authority.",
    "Source WorkspaceFileOwner holds its no-follow regular single-link file descriptor through the complete raw callback, bounds at64MiB and performs metadata/version/path checks around acknowledgement without reading contents. Failed close retains the exact descriptor and blocks new effects until genuine drain retry.",
    "Independent optional artifactClipboard requires actual native host/current UI. Missing capability or source returns unavailable. Public modes retain legacy image/path DTOs, while this private native callback permits onlyfile/unavailable.",
    "An original-active-guard UUID exists only during the raw callback. Native blocking work checks it before scheduling publication and after actual GTK closure retirement. Forged, retired, cancelled or changed scope tickets refuse; GTK callbacks never block on Source RPC or filesystem reads.",
    "GTK set_with_owner publishes fixed bounded percent-encoded text/uri-list bytes from the captured native path. The opaque GObject payload services future clipboard requests without filesystem authority. Document identity is checked around the actual GTK effect.",
    "Public timeout/drop revokes later effects while actual blocking work/GTK closure remains owned. Shutdown drains accepted work, clears only a matching actual clipboard owner token, waits persistent payload retirement and releases the held root.",
    "Renderer hydration/current-document ingress reject stale results without replay. Read/Scan remain available independently of clipboard support."
  ],
